# AUTHOR-tier dispatcher filter rules
# Deploy to: dispatcher/src/conf.dispatcher.d/filters/ referenced by the *.author.farm
# (NOT the publish filter.any — this is the author farm)
#
# Symptom this fixes:
#   "Forbidden — Cannot serve request to
#    /content/.../jcr:content/root/section/form_XXXXXXXX/ on this server"
#   when saving an AEM Forms component in the Universal Editor.
#
# Root cause (confirmed via Network tab):
#   - Normal UE components (text, image, etc.) persist via Adobe's hosted
#     Universal Editor Service: POST https://universal-editor-service.adobe.io/patch
#     (never touches the author CDN directly — always works).
#   - The AEM Forms component instead does a DIRECT browser->author POST:
#       POST https://author-pXXXXX-eXXXXX.adobeaemcloud.com/content/.../form_XXXXXXXX
#     This hits the author CDN/dispatcher filter, which denies it by default.
#
# This snippet is a WORKAROUND that allows the direct form-node write.
# The root-cause fix is to make the Forms component persist via the UE
# service like other components (see docs/setup/universal-editor-cors.md).

# Allow direct Universal Editor form-node persistence POSTs to author
/0150 { /type "allow" /method "POST" /url "/content/*/jcr:content/root/section/form_*" }
/0151 { /type "allow" /method "POST" /url "/content/*/jcr:content/*/form_*" }
